1
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:41,280
How dare he tell the teacher, that nerd.

2
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:43,759
Isn't that annoying?

3
00:01:44,039 --> 00:01:45,880
But since the teacher has spoken,

4
00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:47,479
we have to show some respect.

5
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:48,660
How about this?

6
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:50,920
You set up a meeting,

7
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:52,759
and I'll make peace with Ma La.

8
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:54,479
You share a dorm with him,

9
00:01:54,479 --> 00:01:55,640
so you ask him out.

10
00:01:57,039 --> 00:01:58,800
Okay, I got it.

11
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:00,080
Then it's settled.

12
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:01,160
Seven o'clock,

13
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:03,120
at the wild beach by the Silver Bridge.

14
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:04,520
If he dares not to show up,

15
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:05,760
I'll kill you.

16
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:09,080
Let's go.

17
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:33,680
Did you notice

18
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:35,480
that Zhiwei's eyes

19
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:37,900
look a bit different from before?

20
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:41,760
Maybe in places we can't see,

21
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:44,560
he did something else.

22
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:47,920
You sound like you know him best.

23
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:50,610
Not as well as you do.

24
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:55,850
I think Xiaotao looks at you differently too.

25
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:57,680
He definitely has a crush on you.

26
00:02:57,680 --> 00:02:58,880
Don't talk nonsense.

27
00:02:59,079 --> 00:03:00,640
Eyes can speak.

28
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:02,800
No one can fool me.

29
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:08,440
Then tell me,

30
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:10,240
who does Zhiwei give

31
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:11,640
the most special look to?

32
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:13,520
Him?

33
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:17,000
He gives Xiaotao the most special look.

34
00:03:25,079 --> 00:03:25,680
Xiaotao,

35
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:27,860
I need your help right now.

36
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:29,240
Listen to me.

37
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:31,720
At this moment,

38
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:34,280
I should be chatting with Lao Dai on the terrace.

39
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:35,079
So,

40
00:03:35,760 --> 00:03:39,360
do you know how many web novelists there are now?

41
00:03:40,079 --> 00:03:41,160
My editor told me

42
00:03:41,640 --> 00:03:42,840
there are 24 million.

43
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:45,720
Plus the endless stream of AI,

44
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:47,530
what does that mean?

45
00:03:47,960 --> 00:03:50,880
So this pie-in-the-sky luck of yours,

46
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:53,400
you might not get it again in your lifetime.

47
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,200
Understood?

48
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:56,000
So, brother,

49
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,000
I'll say it again.

50
00:03:57,760 --> 00:03:59,040
Don't be too greedy.

51
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,280
Take what you have.

52
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:02,240
Understood?

53
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:05,840
You died at 10:00.

54
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,200
And I died at 12:00.

55
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:07,760
What?

56
00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:09,800
We both died?

57
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:14,620
Mala left me a clue and a meteorite necklace,

58
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:17,440
pointing to a sentence in 'The Death of Marat'.

59
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,399
The only one with a motive to kill

60
00:04:19,399 --> 00:04:20,360
could be him.

61
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:26,160
I know that whatever I say now,

62
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:27,420
no one will believe me,

63
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:29,200
just like Mala back then.

64
00:04:30,320 --> 00:04:32,520
And before I time-traveled, I found out

65
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:34,440
that something might happen to An'an too.

66
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:35,800
What happened to An'an?

67
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:38,980
I don't know what happened to her.

68
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:41,320
But these causes and effects,

69
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:43,120
I can't tell Sophie and An'an,

70
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:45,200
let alone Old Dai.

71
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:48,520
You're the only one I can rely on now.

72
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:49,880
Help me

73
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:52,930
get everyone out of here alive.

74
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:57,370
I was the one who called him over back then.

75
00:04:57,880 --> 00:04:59,810
I indirectly caused Mala's death.

76
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:02,600
He wants revenge on me.

77
00:05:03,520 --> 00:05:04,780
I can understand that.

78
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:08,440
But why would he want to harm you?

79
00:05:11,760 --> 00:05:13,000
Let's find him first.

80
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:33,330
We're still a step too late.

81
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:35,330
At least we're still alive.

82
00:05:35,520 --> 00:05:36,720
What should we do now?

83
00:05:43,960 --> 00:05:45,290
Is the Mala you remember

84
00:05:45,840 --> 00:05:47,880
capable of murder?

85
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:56,040
We wrote about his painful experiences

86
00:05:56,040 --> 00:05:57,159
to make money.

87
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:59,360
Would he be indifferent to that?

88
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:04,170
Is he still holding a grudge against me

89
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:06,920
for calling him out that night?

90
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:09,840
But brother, you know I didn't mean it.

91
00:06:11,080 --> 00:06:11,920
I'm scared.

92
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:15,620
I'm scared I'll end up like those who bullied him back then.

93
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:17,010
They didn't end up well.

94
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:20,650
What kind of person is Mala?

95
00:06:20,720 --> 00:06:22,450
Maybe we never really knew him.

96
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:35,880
Breaking up and getting back together.

97
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:38,940
Let's just part on good terms.

98
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:47,800
Wait.

99
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:48,640
What's wrong?

100
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:49,960
Aren't we going to stop him?

101
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:51,640
The other me is going to chase him soon.

102
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:54,770
Time travelers can't come face to face with themselves.

103
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:55,800
What's wrong?

104
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:57,200
Help take care of Mr. Dai.

105
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:04,800
Xiaotao, whatever you do, don't go to the room upstairs.

106
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:05,640
Got it?

107
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:08,240
Uncle Dai.

108
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:09,920
Over there. That's your room.

109
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,260
It's fine. No problem.

110
00:07:13,440 --> 00:07:13,840
Slow down.

111
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:16,440
I can take care of myself. It's fine.

112
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:18,520
Xiaotao! Xiaotao, come up and help me quickly.

113
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:20,000
Okay, I'm coming.

114
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:22,360
Don't trust anyone but me.

115
00:07:22,720 --> 00:07:24,880
I'll give you an explanation for what happened to you.

116
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:25,800
Be careful.

117
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:29,560
Xiaotao, Uncle Dai just threw up all over himself.

118
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:31,040
Remember to help him clean up.

119
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:32,040
No need, Xiaotao.

120
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:33,560
It's fine.

121
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:38,860
Zhiwei just rushed out suddenly.

122
00:07:38,920 --> 00:07:40,040
I don't know what happened.

123
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:41,000
It startled me.

124
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:44,000
Mr. Dai, this way.

125
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,200
Excuse me.

126
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:18,160
It's almost ten o'clock.

127
00:08:18,840 --> 00:08:19,800
At ten o'clock,

128
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:22,320
Xiaotao was pushed off the balcony of this room

129
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:23,440
by a man in black.

130
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:27,160
It's very likely that the man in black is hiding in this room,

131
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:27,720
or

132
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:29,800
is on his way here.
